{
  "$schema": "../../scenario.schema.json",
  "id": "memory/a-split-mark-keeps-memory-speaker-labels",
  "title": "A split runtime mark never strips a speaker label from a memory message, within memory or at its boundary with the turn",
  "rules": [
    "§6.4",
    "§20.2"
  ],
  "requirements": [
    "RK-20.2-002",
    "RK-20.2-003",
    "RK-20.2-006"
  ],
  "notes": "Python tests/test_runtime_mark_copies.py::test_a_split_copy_never_takes_a_labelled_message_s_label and the public MockMemoryProvider witness from the ScriptExecutor integration review. Messages whose metadata contains speaker stop the split-copy scan. They are not pieces of an unlabelled mark. The final user memory text still joins the input as the memory contract specifies.",
